      "pageDescription": "",
      "evidenceText": "Harvard Kennedy School (HKS) American Service Fellowship 2027 (up to $100,000) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Wednesday, November 11 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Harvard Kennedy School (HKS) American Service Fellowship 2027 (up to $100,000) Jude Ogar November 11, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: December 1, 2026 Applications are invited for the Harvard Kennedy School (HKS) American Service Fellowship 2027 . The American Service Fellowship offers a full scholarship and a partial living stipend for U.S. public servants to enroll in the one-year, on-campus Mid-Career Master in Public Administration (MC/MPA) Program at Harvard Kennedy School. This fellowship honors your service and helps you take the next step in your public leadership journey. You will learn from world-class Harvard Kennedy School faculty members, get the best public policy education in the world, and join a powerful network of change makers from across the country—each bringing a unique story, perspective, and commitment to impact. Most of all, you’ll learn how to tackle the biggest challenges and lead the country into the future. Program Highlights Customizable curriculum Mid-career peer cohort with a demonstrated commitment to public service Access to Harvard-wide resources Career support and leadership development Benefits A $100,000 scholarship for public servants pursuing the Mid-Career Master in Public Administration, covering full tuition and fees plus a partial living stipend. Eligibility You may be a strong fit if you: Have a minimum of 7 years of public service experience in the United States, regardless of your nationality; Demonstrate excellent leadership skills and a track record of academic and professional achievement; Are ready to dedicate a year to full-time study on our campus in Cambridge, Massachusetts; Want to bring what you learn back to your community. Selection Criteria Applications will be reviewed holistically with attention paid to: Academic and intellectual potential Professional achievements and leadership Public service motivation and values Application Application to the Harvard Kennedy School will close on December 1, 2026 at 12 p.m. (noon) ET. Click here to apply For more information, visit HKS American Service Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Africa Dyslexia Teacher Fellowship Program 2027 Next Article ANH Academy Science-Policy Fellowships 2027 (Round 3) Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts ANH Academy Science-Policy Fellowships 2027 (Round 3) November 11, 2026 Closes in 474 days Africa Dyslexia Teacher Fellowship Program 2027 November 11, 2026 Closes in 9 days Pladis Accelerator Programme 2026 November 11, 2026 Closes in 65 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts ANH Academy Science-Policy Fellowships 2027 (Round 3) Harvard Kennedy School (HKS) American Service Fellowship 2027 (up to $100,000) Africa Dyslexia Teacher Fellowship Program 2027 Pladis Accelerator Programme 2026 African Development Bank Group Shanghai Ocean University Scholarship Masters Degree Program 2027 Global Youth Mental Health Research Fellowship 2027 Commonwealth Shared Scholarship Programme 2027/2028 to Study in the U.K. (Fully-funded) African Wildlife Foundation (AWF) Geospatial Leaders Fellowship 2027 Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
