ntials for New Editors (January 2027) quantity Enroll Now Reporting & Editing Online Edit to Elevate: Essentials for New Editors (January 2027) Transform your editing from transactional to transformational with program lead Tom Huang and industry veterans Maria Carrillo, Tony Elkins and Kathleen McGrory. Learn to line edit under pressure, coach inexperienced reporters and help your reporters develop quick enterprise stories that elevate their beat coverage. Earn a certificate of completion to demonstrate your editing skills and professional development. January 13, 2027 &ndash; February 10, 2027 Overview Space is limited and this program will sell out. Enroll by Jan. 8, 2027 or before seats fill. Join five weekly, 90-minute online sessions from Jan. 13 to Feb. 10, 2027. Designed for new editors in their first three to five years, across all journalism platforms. Learn from Tom Huang, Maria Carrillo, Tony Elkins and Kathleen McGrory. Practice new techniques through interactive sessions with opportunities to ask questions. Connect with a supportive community of fellow editors to exchange ideas and experiences. Access session replays and practical resources to continue learning at your own pace. Earn a Poynter certificate of completion to demonstrate your professional development. In stock Edit to Elevate: Essentials for New Editors (January 2027) quantity Enroll Now SKU: 82706 Tags: Certificate , Editing , front page course , Online group seminar , Reporting and Editing , Tom Huang Learning Outcomes By the end of this course, you will: Strengthen your line editing skills, especially under tight deadlines. Develop a strong sense of mission and purpose as an editor. Adopt a coaching mindset to guide reporters rather than simply correct their work. Help reporters sharpen their story focus, structure and clarity. Coach reporters to develop ambitious enterprise stories from their beats. Apply project management techniques to coordinate teams and newsroom initiatives. Build effective working relationships with reporters in hybrid and remote newsrooms. Sale New Certificate $ 650.00 Original price was: $650.00. $ 499.00 Current price is: $499.00. In stock Edit to Elevate: Essentials for New Editors (January 2027) quantity Enroll Now Overview Space is limited and this program will sell out. Enroll by Jan. 8, 2027 or before seats fill. Join five weekly, 90-minute online sessions from Jan. 13 to Feb. 10, 2027. Designed for new editors in their first three to five years, across all journalism platforms. Learn from Tom Huang, Maria Carrillo, Tony Elkins and Kathleen McGrory. Practice new techniques through interactive sessions with opportunities to ask questions. Connect with a supportive community of fellow editors to exchange ideas and experiences. Access session replays and practical resources to continue learning at your own pace. Earn a Poynter certificate of completion to demonstrate your professional development. Training 5 or More People? get consulting & coaching Description Schedule Requirements Today’s newsrooms are increasingly younger, smaller, short on resources and operating remotely. Editors face a unique set of challenges: managing reporters they rarely see in person, providing direction to writers scattered across locations and coaching journalists who lack mentorship. They also need guidance and a community of fellow editors who understand these challenges and can offer support. Apply if you’re a new editor looking to build confidence, sharpen your skills and connect with a supportive community of peers This five-week, skills-intensive course is designed to help new editors move beyond the basics to focus on the mission, mindset and roadmap required to make them indispensable to their newsrooms. Along the way, they’ll build connections with fellow editors, receive guidance from experienced journalists and earn a certificate of completion to demonstrate their professional growth. What will you learn? Get practical training via weekly sessions from program lead Tom Huang and accomplished journalists and editors Maria Carrillo and Kathleen McGrory. Plus, Poynter faculty Tony Elkins will teach a session about project management for editors. This program delivers tools to strengthen your line editing skills and provides the support you need to build a strong sense of mission and purpose as an editor. You’ll gain the confidence to actively coach rather than passively edit, learn methods for improving story structure and focus and grasp how to help reporters find compelling angles they can execute with speed and quality. Why learn with Poynter? The Poynter Institute is a global nonprofit working to address society’s most pressing issues by teaching journalists and journalism, covering the media and the complexities facing the industry, convening and community building, improving the capacity and sustainability of news organizations and fostering trust and reliability of information. The world’s top journalists and emerging media leaders rely on the Institute to learn new skills, adopt best practices, better serve audiences, scale operations and improve the quality of the universally shared information ecosystem. Space is limited and this program will sell out. Enroll by Jan. 8, 2027 or before seats fill. Questions? If you need assistance, email us at info@poynter.org . Wednesday, Jan. 13, 2027, 2-3:30 p.m. Eastern Hands on editing (Session leaders: Tom Huang, Maria Carrillo, Kat McGrory) Get the tools to line edit stories to elevate them. You’ll be equipped with actionable tips on “triage” editing for tight deadlines and identify and troubleshoot strategies for story strengths and weaknesses. Wednesday, Jan. 20, 2027, 2-3:30 p.m. Eastern Building your team (Session leader: Tom Huang) Learn key techniques for building your team on a daily basis – what are practical steps you can take starting now? Discover how to be intentional about your time in the newsroom when you’re in a hybrid workplace. Employ key tips for collaborating across teams – understanding that getting things done is based on building relationships across the newsroom – and not just when you need something on deadline. Wednesday, Jan. 27, 2027, 2-3:30 p.m. Eastern Editing without your hands (Session leader: Maria Carrillo) Delve into the art of establishing a coaching relationship with your reporters. Learn how to spark ideas for stories and push reporters to vet, elevate and focus them. You’ll build your toolkit of strategic questions, learn how to say “no” without dampening ambitions and coach in a hybrid work environment. Wednesday, Feb. 3, 2027, 2-3:30 p.m. Eastern Project management (Session leader: Tony Elkins) Develop tools to lead projects for your team and across your newsroom. Wednesday, Feb. 10, 2027, 2-3:30 p.m. Eastern Ambitious editing (Session leader: Kathleen McGrory) Coach reporters to bring ambition and enterprise thinking to their beats through short-range and mid-range story development. Sharpen focus, frame, clarity, and organization while helping reporters bulletproof their work. Who should enroll? This course is designed for newer editors in their first three to five years on the job, across digital, print, broadcast and multimedia platforms, who are looking to strengthen their skills, gain confidence and connect with a supportive journalism community. Experienced editors who want to refresh their line editing and coaching skills will also benefit. Whether you work in a small local newsroom or a large national organization, in public or private media, this program addresses the challenges editors face in today’s evolving media landscape. Editors from diverse backgrounds who are eager to grow, learn from industry experts and exchange ideas and experiences with their peers are encouraged to join. Enroll by Jan. 8 2027 to secure your spot. Cost $499 for five 90-minute online sessions with leading journalism experts. You’ll also get access to session replays, practical resources and a supportive community of fellow editors. Space is intentionally limited so you can get your questions answered and connect directly with instructors. Upon completion, you’ll earn a certificate to demonstrate your editing skills and professional development. Instructors Lead Faculty Tom Huang Assistant Managing Editor for Journalism Initiatives, The Dallas Morning News Tom Huang is Assistant Managing Editor for Journalism Initiatives at The Dallas Morning News, where he edits stories across multiple beats, oversees the newsroom’s internship and... Read More Contributing Faculty Maria Carrillo Consultant and retired Tampa Bay Times editor Maria Carrillo retired as senior deputy editor of the Tampa Bay Times. She worked as senior deputy editor of the Houston Chronicle and, before that,... Read More Tony Elkins Poynter Faculty Tony Elkins is a faculty member at Poynter. His portfolio includes Poynter’s leadership workshops Essential Skills for Rising Newsroom Leaders and the Leadership Academy for... Read More Kathleen McGrory Editor, New York Times Local Investigations Fellowship Kathleen McGrory is an editor for the New York Times’ Local Investigations Fellowship program. She was previously a reporter on ProPublica’s national staff. Before that,... Read More \"> Related Products Sale Certificate Online Poynter ACES Introductory Certificate in Editing $ 300.00 Original price was: $300.00. $ 150.00 Current price is: $150.00. Free Certificate Online Poynter ACES Advanced Certificate in Editing Final Assessment $ 0.00 Sale Apply by Jan 8, 2027 Online Lead with Influence (February 2027) $ 599.00 Original price was: $599.00. $ 499.00 Current price is: $499.00. Online Connecting the Dots: Developmental Editing for Structure, Character and Flow $ 125.00",
